Each of the following lines of code generates an error message when we invoke the assembler. Explain what is wrong with each line.

movb $0xF, (%ebx)       --> moving a nibble instead of a byte to a 32 bit memory location
movl %rax, (%rsp)       --> moving a 64 bit value in a register using the double word instruction
movw (%rax),4(%rsp)     --> moving a 64 bit value in memory using the word instruction
